WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.480
How does Dijkstra’s algorithm work?

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.780
Repeatedly settle the smallest tentative

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.840
distance, then relax its outgoing

4
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.600
edges. The guarantee requires nonnegative

5
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.860
edge weights, including zero; a

6
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.120
negative edge is enough to

7
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:13.520
break it.

8
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.480
Set the source S to

9
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.580
zero, other distances to infinity,

10
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.300
and keep an indexed min-heap

11
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.960
keyed by tentative distance. A

12
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.600
parent records the route responsible

13
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.100
for each improvement; discovering a

14
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.340
route does not yet settle

15
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.280
its destination.

16
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.120
Settle S first. Its edges

17
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.780
offer A distance four and

18
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.760
B distance one, so update

19
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.400
those queue keys and parents;

20
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.420
B is now the smallest

21
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.640
unsettled candidate.

22
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.600
Settle B at one. Via

23
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.680
B, A improves from four

24
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.560
to three, and T receives

25
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.080
a tentative nine; decrease A’s

26
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.460
queue key instead of leaving

27
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.660
the old priority behind.

28
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.540
Next settle A at three.

29
00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.820
Its edge to T offers

30
00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.540
three plus two, improving nine

31
00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.740
to five; update T’s parent

32
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.420
to A and lower its

33
00:01:03.427 --> 00:01:03.900
queue key.

34
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.560
Finally settle T at five.

35
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.140
Following parents backwards gives T,

36
00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.140
A, B, S, so the

37
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.720
route S, B, A, T

38
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.500
costs one plus two plus

39
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.240
two, which is five.

40
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.520
Every settled label is optimal.

41
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.320
If a cheaper route to

42
00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.460
the extracted minimum existed, its

43
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:24.580
first unsettled vertex would already

44
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.700
have been offered a no-larger

45
00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.720
prefix cost by its settled

46
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.940
predecessor; nonnegative remaining edges preserve

47
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:31.840
that comparison.

48
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.920
See why negative edges matter:

49
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.880
S to A costs one,

50
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.960
S to B costs two,

51
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.680
and B to A costs

52
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.100
negative three. A could settle

53
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.860
at one before B reveals

54
00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.640
the true distance negative one,

55
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.460
even without any cycle.

56
00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.760
An indexed binary heap extracts

57
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.500
each vertex at most once

58
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.200
and performs at most one

59
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.640
successful decrease-key per scanned edge.

60
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.240
With logarithmic heap operations, the

61
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.740
total is order n plus

62
00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.740
m, times log n, using

63
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.760
adjacency lists.

64
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.380
Labels, parents, membership flags, and

65
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.060
an indexed heap use order

66
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.380
n auxiliary space. A lazy

67
00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.760
duplicate-entry queue needs separate accounting

68
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.420
and must skip stale entries;

69
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.940
it is not the same

70
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.760
queue implementation.

71
00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.120
Things to take note of.

72
00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:22.840
Stop once the target is

73
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.620
settled for a single-target query,

74
00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.340
or once the smallest remaining

75
00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.360
label is infinite. Equal-distance routes

76
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.540
may choose different parents; strict

77
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.060
improvement keeps unnecessary parent changes

78
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:34.400
out.

79
00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.660
For a one-vertex graph, the

80
00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.757
source distance is zero; an

81
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.040
empty graph has no valid

82
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.380
chosen source. Keep tentative labels

83
00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.220
separate from settled facts, and

84
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.840
never smuggle a negative edge

85
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.200
into the assumptions. Hmph, even

86
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.400
greed needs a proof.
